h('15. Recorded evaluation and measured limitations')
p('The following are saved repository results, not experiments rerun for this report. Different suites correspond to different implementation stages.','c')
sub('15.1 FABC and database evaluation')
table([['Measure','Recorded result'],['FABC implementation-stage tests','122 passed, 1 PostgreSQL-dependent skip'],['Synthetic scenario study','1,200 targets; FABC precision 39.25%, recall 42.00%; 130 false alerts per 1,000 benign targets'],['SQLite replay benchmark','100 transfers, 100 persisted certificates, all replayed'],['Ledger/certificate workload latency','p50 / p95 / p99: 20.20 / 22.01 / 22.46 ms'],['Control latency','17.11 / 18.29 / 18.53 ms; disables both ledger and certificate writes'],['Sequential throughput','49.05 transfers/s with evidence; 57.75 transfers/s control'],['Indexed history plan','Used idx_ledger_account_recorded_seq']],[176,311])
p('This is a warm-model sequential local SQLite workload, not PostgreSQL lock-wait or concurrent throughput validation. Combined ledger/certificate overhead is measured, not certificate-only overhead. Synthetic benign collections can resemble suspicious histories; haircut achieved higher recall and average precision in this constructed study. The ML comparison on synthetic snapshots is a domain-mismatch stress test.')
sub('15.2 Historical PaySim comparison')
p('A seeded 2% sample contained 127,171 rows: 117,936 train (91 fraud), 5,401 validation (34 fraud), and 3,834 test (38 fraud). Validation starts at step 404; test at 564. Thresholds are selected on validation only.')
table([['Model','Test TP / FN / FP','Precision / recall / F1'],['Transaction Random Forest','38 / 0 / 0','1.000 / 1.000 / 1.000'],['Historical-graph Random Forest','36 / 2 / 0','1.000 / 0.9474 / 0.9730']],[170,130,187])
p('The small sampled test does not establish generalization or a graph improvement. Both methods had 3,796 true negatives. The historical graph is sampled rather than a complete banking network.')
sub('15.3 Joint prototype validation')
p('The recorded full suite passed 394 tests with one skip; 272 new tests included 250 generated ledgers matching exhaustive integer allocation. Joint analysis including verification had p50/p95 0.4281/0.4964 ms. In 100 deliberately simple one-query cases, proposed selection and reachability filtering resolved 100/100, widest-boundary 0/100, and seeded random 40/100. These are proof-of-concept results, not fraud accuracy or real analyst workload.')
page()
h('16. Interface, deployment and project demonstration')
sub('16.1 User-facing modules and API')
p('Banking provides customer/account/device registration, transfers, history filters, stored predictions, alert review, customer profiles and FABC inspection/replay. DBMS Demonstration exposes objects, audit history, query plans, rollback and concurrency examples. Original Overview, Fraud Detection, Graph Explorer, Model Performance and Explainability pages display batch outputs.')
p('API groups include /customers, /accounts, /devices, /transactions, /fraud/alerts, /fraud/statistics, /audit-logs and /database/overview, alongside the certificate routes. Alert reviews update workflow status without changing certified financial facts. Development demonstration routes are omitted when APP_ENV=production; this does not add authentication.')
sub('16.2 Docker and local setup')
p('Docker Hub repository: <link href="https://hub.docker.com/r/sayantarat/frauddetectai" color="black">https://hub.docker.com/r/sayantarat/frauddetectai</link>. The Compose backend image is sayantarat/frauddetectai:latest and also supports a local build. PostgreSQL uses a named persistent volume. Both backend and database ports bind to localhost.')
code('docker pull sayantarat/frauddetectai:latest\n# From the project directory, with a compatible model in ./models:\ndocker compose up -d postgres\ndocker compose up -d backend\n# Alternative: docker compose up --build -d\n\n# Host Python environment:\nexport PYTHONPATH=src:.\n# Set DATABASE_URL for the selected database.\nalembic upgrade head\npython scripts/seed_database.py\nuvicorn app.main:app --reload\n# Second terminal:\nstreamlit run app/streamlit_app.py')
p('Compose starts migrations before Uvicorn and mounts ./models read-only. A raw standalone docker run is insufficient without a configured database and fitted model. For SQLite, use DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///data/banking.db. PostgreSQL is required for row locks, JSONB and SQL-function demonstrations. The image was not pulled or executed as part of preparing this report.')
sub('16.3 Concise presentation sequence')
for t in ['Show the customer/account relationship and submit a valid transfer.','Open the stored probability, behaviour score and alert; explain their distinction.','Inspect the FABC interval, evidence sequence and replay result.','Demonstrate rollback after an injected essential failure, then concurrent debits.','Run the offline joint-funding example and compare individual versus collective bounds.','End with measured limitations rather than claiming production detection superiority.']:bullet(t)
page()
h('17. Contribution, limitations and conclusion')
sub('17.1 Defensible contribution')
p('The implemented contribution is an uncertainty-aware banking evidence workflow: attainable funding bounds, a validated ordered ledger prefix, atomic persistence with a transfer, retained evidence and replay. The offline extension investigates joint source-cohort holdings and cost-aware evidence acquisition. The mathematical constituents, database locks and hashes should not individually be described as inventions. Global originality and patent novelty remain unresolved; no new patent assessment was performed for this report.')
sub('17.2 Remaining limitations and future work')
for t in ['The course application has no implemented authentication; production authorization, secrets management and operational controls remain necessary.','The pre-FABC validation records PostgreSQL checks, but the later FABC/joint runs do not establish execution of the new PostgreSQL triggers, row-lock performance or server-restart recovery.','All movement writers must obey account locks and ledger conservation. Administrator bypass and arbitrary direct balance updates are outside the evidence guarantee.','PaySim and designed synthetic scenarios do not validate real-bank behaviour, minute-level funding policies, calibrated online probabilities or broad generalization.','The joint prototype remains offline and restricted to its complete-ledger input contract. Stronger connected-path benchmarks, realistic evidence costs and query complementarity remain future research.','Incremental window-expiry maintenance, learned evidence value, online graph adaptation, GNNs and SHAP explanations are not implemented contributions of this report.']:bullet(t)
sub('17.3 Conclusion')
p('FraudDetectAI demonstrates how banking transaction integrity, AI risk assessment and funding explanations can coexist in a single project. Its strongest result is reproducible, explicitly bounded evidence rather than a claim that suspicious funding proves fraud. The application integrates FABC with the transfer transaction; the offline prototype extends the investigation to collective account holdings. Recorded tests and benchmarks support feasibility within stated assumptions, while showing where detection and deployment claims remain limited.')
sub('18. Sources and reproducibility')
p('Primary implementation sources: app/db/models.py; app/db/objects.py; app/api/routes.py; app/services/transactions.py, inference.py, features.py, flow_bounds.py, flow_evidence.py and joint_funding.py; alembic/versions/; src/fraudgraph/features/historical_graph.py; docker-compose.yml; Dockerfile.','c')
p('Recorded evidence: docs/COMPLETION_AUDIT.md; docs/VALIDATION.md (earlier stage); docs/JOINT_FUNDING_PROTOTYPE.md; docs/evaluation/flow_evaluation.json, flow_database_benchmark.json, historical_graph_evaluation.json and joint_funding_evaluation.json. Reproduction entry points: scripts/evaluate_flow.py, benchmark_flow_database.py, evaluate_historical_graph.py, evaluate_joint_funding.py and run_joint_funding.py.','c')
p('Structural reference: supplied 24BKT0104_VL2026270101632_CS1.pdf. Its proposed architecture/schema are superseded here by the current implementation. The author names and registration numbers are retained. Docker repository URL was supplied by the project owner. This report updates implementation facts without repeating the earlier report\'s unverified legal or prior-art assertions.','c')

